      "ReviewText": "I  picked up this mower despite it not having very many reviews.  It has obstacle avoidance so it can navigate around objects in the yard but it will also go around tall weeds so just be aware of that limitation when first starting.\n\nAfter laying and staking the wire and following the mower around the yard to fix any wire placement issues, it's been working really well.  \n\nThe mower seems to bounce around randomly over the yard but after a few days of mowing it should have perfect coverage. My wife seems amused at the haphazard style but the mower is cheaper than paying someone to do it for a season and greatly reduces the need to be out mowing on a hot summer day. 0 emissions is a side benefit.\n\nThe mower will not 100% eliminate your need to mow, but it does greatly reduce the need to mow.  I have 1 section of my yard that the mower can't access due to a fence so I still need to mow it.  I'm already planning on running border wire across the driveway to mow the other side of my front yard which is not fenced further reducing my mowing effort.  I estimate that my personal mowing time will go from 1.5 hours to less than 30 mins.  Edging the lawn  is still required.",
      "Title": "Working great. Boundary wire was easy to install",
      "UserNickname": "pickandpray",
